module

public import MMP.Attr
public import MMP.AlgebraicGeometry.Divisor.Principal
public import Mathlib.Algebra.Order.Floor.Ring
public import Mathlib.RingTheory.Length
public import StacksFrontier.AlgebraicGeometry.Scheme.QuasiCoherent.IdealSheafStalkSupport

/-!
# Arithmetic of divisors with coefficients

This file collects the elementary operations on divisors with coefficients of Kollár–Mori,
Notation 0.4, and the constructions of later chapters built from them.

An `ℝ`-divisor `D = ∑ dᵢ Dᵢ` is *effective* if every `dᵢ ≥ 0`, and `A ≥ B` means that `A - B` is
effective. Its *round down*, *round up* and *fractional part* are taken coefficientwise:
`⌊D⌋ = ∑ ⌊dᵢ⌋ Dᵢ`, `⌈D⌉ = ∑ ⌈dᵢ⌉ Dᵢ` and `{D} = ∑ {dᵢ} Dᵢ`. Two `ℚ`-divisors are
*`ℚ`-linearly equivalent* if a positive multiple of their difference is a principal divisor.

The *multiplicity* `mult_x P` of a prime divisor `P` at a point `x` is the largest `k` with
`(I_P)_x ⊆ 𝔪_x^k`, and `mult_x D = ∑ dᵢ mult_x Dᵢ`.

For a morphism `f : S ⟶ X` (typically the inclusion of a closed subscheme) and a prime divisor
`P` of `S`, the *local intersection length* of a prime divisor `E` of `X` along `P` is the length
of the `𝒪_{S,P}`-module `𝒪_{S,P}/I_E 𝒪_{S,P}`, and the *restriction* of `D = ∑ dᵢ Dᵢ` to `S` is
`D|_S = ∑_P (∑ᵢ dᵢ · length(𝒪_{S,P}/I_{Dᵢ}𝒪_{S,P})) P`. The *restriction by components*
`Δ|_H` instead has coefficient `∑_{j : C ⊆ Dⱼ} aⱼ` at a prime divisor `C` of `H`.

Finally the space `Div(X)_K` of *`K`-Cartier divisors* is the free `K`-module on the Cartier
divisors, and a `ℚ`-Cartier `ℚ`-divisor `D` with Cartier index `m_D` has the *associated
`ℚ`-Cartier divisor* `⟨D⟩ = (1/m_D) · (m_D D)`.

## Main definitions

* `MMP.Mori.DivisorWithCoeffs.IsEffective`: effective divisors; the order `B ≤ A` is that of
  finitely supported functions (`MMP.Mori.DivisorWithCoeffs.le_iff_isEffective_sub`).
* `MMP.Mori.DivisorWithCoeffs.roundDown`, `MMP.Mori.DivisorWithCoeffs.roundUp`,
  `MMP.Mori.DivisorWithCoeffs.fract`: `⌊D⌋`, `⌈D⌉`, `{D}`, on top of `Int.floor`, `Int.ceil`,
  `Int.fract`.
* `MMP.Mori.QDivisor.QLinearlyEquivalent`: `D₁ ∼_ℚ D₂`.
* `MMP.Mori.localMultiplicity`, `MMP.Mori.PrimeDivisor.multiplicityAt`,
  `MMP.Mori.DivisorWithCoeffs.multiplicityAt`: `mult_x g`, `mult_x P`, `mult_x D`.
* `MMP.Mori.PrimeDivisor.intersectionLength`, `MMP.Mori.DivisorWithCoeffs.restrict`,
  `MMP.Mori.DivisorWithCoeffs.restrictPrimeDivisor`,
  `MMP.Mori.DivisorWithCoeffs.localIntersectionNumber`: `Dᵢ|_S`, `D|_S`, `B|_F`, `(D · Δ)_x`.
* `MMP.Mori.DivisorWithCoeffs.restrictComponents`: `Δ|_H`.
* `MMP.Mori.CartierDivisorWithCoeffs`, with `MMP.Mori.CartierDivisorWithCoeffs.ofCartier` and
  `MMP.Mori.CartierDivisorWithCoeffs.realization`: `Div(X)_K`.
* `MMP.Mori.QDivisor.associatedCartier`: `⟨D⟩`.

## Main results

* `MMP.Mori.DivisorWithCoeffs.roundDown_add_fract`: `D = ⌊D⌋ + {D}`.
* `MMP.Mori.QDivisor.qLinearlyEquivalent_equivalence`: `∼_ℚ` is an equivalence relation.
* `MMP.Mori.PrimeDivisor.multiplicityAt_eq_zero_of_notMem`: `mult_x P = 0` for `x ∉ P`, and
  `MMP.Mori.PrimeDivisor.multiplicityAt_eq_localMultiplicity`: `mult_x P = mult_x g` for a local
  equation `g` of `P` at `x`.
* `MMP.Mori.DivisorWithCoeffs.finite_support_restrictCoeff`: the restriction has finite support when
  no point of `S` of coheight zero maps into a component of `D`, and
  `MMP.Mori.DivisorWithCoeffs.coeff_restrictPrimeDivisor`: this holds for the restriction to a
  prime divisor `F` which is not a component of `D`.
* `MMP.Mori.QDivisor.toDivisorWithCoeffs_associatedCartier`: `⟨D⟩` is `D` again as a
  `ℚ`-divisor.

## Implementation notes

The order on divisors is the coefficientwise order of `Finsupp`, which is the order of the
source: `B ≤ A` exactly when `A - B` is effective.

The restrictions are defined along an arbitrary morphism `f : S ⟶ X`; the source restricts to
the inclusion of a smooth prime divisor (KM 3.10), of a reduced divisor along whose prime
divisors `X` and `S` are regular (KM 5.46–5.63), or of a normal subscheme of pure codimension
one (KM 5.17). In the second setting the source writes the coefficient of `P` through local
equations `gᵢ` of the components `Dᵢ` at `η_P` as `∑ dᵢ v_P(gᵢ|_S)`; since `I_{Dᵢ}` is generated
by `gᵢ` at `η_P`, `𝒪_{S,P}/I_{Dᵢ}𝒪_{S,P} = 𝒪_{S,P}/(gᵢ|_S)`, whose length is `v_P(gᵢ|_S)`
for the discrete valuation ring `𝒪_{S,P}`, so the two definitions agree. The lengths are
finite in all these settings, and are read in `ℕ` through `ENat.toNat`. The finiteness of the
support of a restriction depends on its hypotheses, so the restriction is the zero divisor
when the support is infinite; `MMP.Mori.DivisorWithCoeffs.coeff_restrict` gives the
coefficients whenever it is finite.

The multiplicity of a prime divisor at a point is defined through its ideal at `x`, which is
generated by a local equation of `P` when `P` is Cartier at `x`; it lies in `ℕ∞`, and is read in
`ℕ` in the multiplicity of a divisor, where it is finite on a smooth variety.

The Cartier divisors of a locally Noetherian normal scheme are the divisors which are Cartier in
the sense of `MMP.Mori.Divisor.IsCartier`, the additive subgroup
`MMP.Mori.Divisor.cartierSubgroup`.

## References

* [J. Kollár, S. Mori, *Birational geometry of algebraic varieties*][KollarMori], Notation 0.4,
  1.17, 1.24, 3.5, 3.10, 4.5, 5.17, 5.46
* [R. Hartshorne, *Algebraic geometry*][Har77], V.3
-/

@[expose] public noncomputable section

open CategoryTheory AlgebraicGeometry TopologicalSpace Order

universe u v

namespace MMP.Mori

variable {X : Scheme.{u}}

namespace DivisorWithCoeffs

/-! ### Effective divisors and the order -/

section Order

variable {R : Type v}

/-- A divisor `D = ∑ dᵢ Dᵢ` with coefficients in an ordered ring (an `ℝ`-divisor, a `ℚ`-divisor
or a divisor) is *effective* if `dᵢ ≥ 0` for every `i`. -/
@[mmp "def_km0_effective_divisor"]
def IsEffective [Zero R] [LE R] (D : DivisorWithCoeffs R X) : Prop :=
  ∀ E : PrimeDivisor X, 0 ≤ D.coeff E

/-- A divisor is effective if and only if it is `≥ 0`. -/
theorem isEffective_iff_nonneg [Zero R] [LE R] {D : DivisorWithCoeffs R X} :
    D.IsEffective ↔ 0 ≤ D := by
  rw [Finsupp.le_def]
  rfl

/-- For divisors `A, B` with coefficients in an ordered group, `B ≤ A` (written also `A ≥ B`)
means that `A - B` is effective. -/
@[mmp "not_km0_divisor_order"]
theorem le_iff_isEffective_sub [AddCommGroup R] [PartialOrder R] [IsOrderedAddMonoid R]
    {A B : DivisorWithCoeffs R X} : B ≤ A ↔ (A - B).IsEffective := by
  rw [isEffective_iff_nonneg, sub_nonneg]

/-- The sum of two effective divisors is effective. -/
theorem IsEffective.add [AddCommMonoid R] [PartialOrder R] [IsOrderedAddMonoid R]
    {D D' : DivisorWithCoeffs R X} (h : D.IsEffective) (h' : D'.IsEffective) :
    (D + D').IsEffective := fun E => add_nonneg (h E) (h' E)

/-- The zero divisor is effective. -/
theorem isEffective_zero [Zero R] [Preorder R] : (0 : DivisorWithCoeffs R X).IsEffective :=
  fun _ => le_rfl

end Order

/-! ### Round down, round up and fractional part -/

/-- A divisor, regarded as a divisor with coefficients in a ring `R`. -/
def ofDivisor (R : Type v) [AddCommGroupWithOne R] : Divisor X →+ DivisorWithCoeffs R X :=
  mapCoeffsAddMonoidHom (Int.castAddHom R)

/-- The coefficient of `E` in a divisor `D` regarded with coefficients in `R` is the image in
`R` of the coefficient of `E` in `D`. -/
@[simp]
theorem coeff_ofDivisor {R : Type v} [AddCommGroupWithOne R] (D : Divisor X) (E : PrimeDivisor X) :
    (ofDivisor R D).coeff E = (D.coeff E : R) := rfl

section Round

variable {R : Type v} [Ring R] [LinearOrder R] [IsOrderedRing R] [FloorRing R]

/-- The *round down* `⌊D⌋ = ∑ ⌊dᵢ⌋ Dᵢ` of a divisor `D = ∑ dᵢ Dᵢ` with real (or rational)
coefficients, a divisor. -/
@[mmp "def_km0_round_down_divisor"]
def roundDown (D : DivisorWithCoeffs R X) : Divisor X :=
  D.mapCoeffs Int.floor Int.floor_zero

/-- The *round up* `⌈D⌉ = ∑ ⌈dᵢ⌉ Dᵢ` of a divisor `D = ∑ dᵢ Dᵢ` with real (or rational)
coefficients, a divisor. -/
@[mmp "def_km0_round_up_divisor"]
def roundUp (D : DivisorWithCoeffs R X) : Divisor X :=
  D.mapCoeffs Int.ceil Int.ceil_zero

/-- The *fractional part* `{D} = ∑ {dᵢ} Dᵢ` of a divisor `D = ∑ dᵢ Dᵢ` with real (or rational)
coefficients. -/
@[mmp "def_km0_fractional_part_divisor"]
def fract (D : DivisorWithCoeffs R X) : DivisorWithCoeffs R X :=
  D.mapCoeffs Int.fract Int.fract_zero

/-- The coefficient of `E` in `⌊D⌋` is `⌊d_E⌋`, for `d_E` the coefficient of `E` in `D`. -/
@[simp]
theorem coeff_roundDown (D : DivisorWithCoeffs R X) (E : PrimeDivisor X) :
    D.roundDown.coeff E = ⌊D.coeff E⌋ :=
  coeff_mapCoeffs Int.floor Int.floor_zero D E

/-- The coefficient of `E` in `⌈D⌉` is `⌈d_E⌉`, for `d_E` the coefficient of `E` in `D`. -/
@[simp]
theorem coeff_roundUp (D : DivisorWithCoeffs R X) (E : PrimeDivisor X) :
    D.roundUp.coeff E = ⌈D.coeff E⌉ :=
  coeff_mapCoeffs Int.ceil Int.ceil_zero D E

/-- The coefficient of `E` in `{D}` is `{d_E}`, for `d_E` the coefficient of `E` in `D`. -/
@[simp]
theorem coeff_fract (D : DivisorWithCoeffs R X) (E : PrimeDivisor X) :
    D.fract.coeff E = Int.fract (D.coeff E) :=
  coeff_mapCoeffs Int.fract Int.fract_zero D E

/-- `D = ⌊D⌋ + {D}`. -/
theorem roundDown_add_fract (D : DivisorWithCoeffs R X) :
    ofDivisor R D.roundDown + D.fract = D := by
  ext E
  simp

/-- `{D} = D - ⌊D⌋`. -/
theorem fract_eq_sub (D : DivisorWithCoeffs R X) : D.fract = D - ofDivisor R D.roundDown := by
  rw [eq_sub_iff_add_eq, add_comm, roundDown_add_fract]

/-- The fractional part `{D}` is effective. -/
theorem isEffective_fract (D : DivisorWithCoeffs R X) : D.fract.IsEffective :=
  fun E => by simp [Int.fract_nonneg]

/-- `⌊D⌋` is the largest divisor below `D`. -/
theorem le_roundDown_iff {D : DivisorWithCoeffs R X} {D' : Divisor X} :
    D' ≤ D.roundDown ↔ ofDivisor R D' ≤ D := by
  simp only [Finsupp.le_def]
  refine forall_congr' fun E => ?_
  change D'.coeff E ≤ D.roundDown.coeff E ↔ (ofDivisor R D').coeff E ≤ D.coeff E
  rw [coeff_roundDown, coeff_ofDivisor]
  exact Int.le_floor

/-- `⌊D⌋ ≤ D`. -/
theorem ofDivisor_roundDown_le (D : DivisorWithCoeffs R X) : ofDivisor R D.roundDown ≤ D :=
  le_roundDown_iff.mp le_rfl

/-- `⌈D⌉` is the smallest divisor above `D`. -/
theorem roundUp_le_iff {D : DivisorWithCoeffs R X} {D' : Divisor X} :
    D.roundUp ≤ D' ↔ D ≤ ofDivisor R D' := by
  simp only [Finsupp.le_def]
  refine forall_congr' fun E => ?_
  change D.roundUp.coeff E ≤ D'.coeff E ↔ D.coeff E ≤ (ofDivisor R D').coeff E
  rw [coeff_roundUp, coeff_ofDivisor]
  exact Int.ceil_le

/-- `D ≤ ⌈D⌉`. -/
theorem le_ofDivisor_roundUp (D : DivisorWithCoeffs R X) : D ≤ ofDivisor R D.roundUp :=
  roundUp_le_iff.mp le_rfl

end Round

end DivisorWithCoeffs

/-! ### Round down, round up and fractional part of a real number

The round down `⌊d⌋ = max {n ∈ ℤ : n ≤ d}` of a real number is `Int.floor`, characterized by
`Int.le_floor : n ≤ ⌊d⌋ ↔ n ≤ d`; the round up `⌈d⌉ = min {n ∈ ℤ : n ≥ d}` is `Int.ceil`,
characterized by `Int.ceil_le : ⌈d⌉ ≤ n ↔ d ≤ n`; and the fractional part `{d} = d - ⌊d⌋` is
`Int.fract`, defined as `d - ⌊d⌋`. -/

/-! ### `ℚ`-linear equivalence -/

namespace QDivisor

section QLinear

variable [IsLocallyNoetherian X] [CompactSpace X] [IsNormal X]

/-- `ℚ`-divisors `D₁, D₂` on a Noetherian normal scheme are *`ℚ`-linearly equivalent*,
`D₁ ∼_ℚ D₂`, if there is an integer `m > 0` such that `m(D₁ - D₂)` is an integral divisor and
`m(D₁ - D₂) = div(φ)` for some unit `φ` of `K(X)`. -/
@[mmp "not_km5b_q_linear_equivalence"]
def QLinearlyEquivalent (D₁ D₂ : QDivisor X) : Prop :=
  ∃ m : ℕ, 0 < m ∧ ∃ φ : (RationalFunctions X)ˣ,
    (m : ℤ) • (D₁ - D₂) = Divisor.toQDivisor (principalDivisor φ)

/-- Every `ℚ`-divisor is `ℚ`-linearly equivalent to itself. -/
@[refl]
theorem QLinearlyEquivalent.refl (D : QDivisor X) : D.QLinearlyEquivalent D :=
  ⟨1, one_pos, 1, by simp [principalDivisor_one]⟩

/-- If `D₁ ∼_ℚ D₂` then `D₂ ∼_ℚ D₁`. -/
@[symm]
theorem QLinearlyEquivalent.symm {D₁ D₂ : QDivisor X} (h : D₁.QLinearlyEquivalent D₂) :
    D₂.QLinearlyEquivalent D₁ := by
  obtain ⟨m, hm, φ, hφ⟩ := h
  refine ⟨m, hm, φ⁻¹, ?_⟩
  rw [principalDivisor_inv, map_neg, ← hφ, ← smul_neg, neg_sub]

/-- If `D₁ ∼_ℚ D₂` and `D₂ ∼_ℚ D₃` then `D₁ ∼_ℚ D₃`. -/
@[trans]
theorem QLinearlyEquivalent.trans {D₁ D₂ D₃ : QDivisor X} (h₁₂ : D₁.QLinearlyEquivalent D₂)
    (h₂₃ : D₂.QLinearlyEquivalent D₃) : D₁.QLinearlyEquivalent D₃ := by
  obtain ⟨m, hm, φ, hφ⟩ := h₁₂
  obtain ⟨n, hn, ψ, hψ⟩ := h₂₃
  refine ⟨m * n, Nat.mul_pos hm hn, φ ^ n * ψ ^ m, ?_⟩
  ext E
  have h1 := congrArg (fun D => DivisorWithCoeffs.coeff D E) hφ
  have h2 := congrArg (fun D => DivisorWithCoeffs.coeff D E) hψ
  simp only [DivisorWithCoeffs.coeff_smul, DivisorWithCoeffs.coeff_sub,
    Divisor.coeff_toQDivisor, coeff_principalDivisor, zsmul_eq_mul] at h1 h2 ⊢
  rw [PrimeDivisor.ord_mul, PrimeDivisor.ord_pow, PrimeDivisor.ord_pow, nsmul_eq_mul,
    nsmul_eq_mul]
  push_cast
  rw [← h1, ← h2]
  push_cast
  ring

/-- `ℚ`-linear equivalence is an equivalence relation on `ℚ`-divisors. -/
theorem qLinearlyEquivalent_equivalence :
    Equivalence (QLinearlyEquivalent (X := X)) :=
  ⟨QLinearlyEquivalent.refl, QLinearlyEquivalent.symm, QLinearlyEquivalent.trans⟩

/-- Linearly equivalent divisors are `ℚ`-linearly equivalent. -/
theorem _root_.MMP.Mori.Divisor.LinearlyEquivalent.qLinearlyEquivalent {D₁ D₂ : Divisor X}
    (h : D₁.LinearlyEquivalent D₂) :
    (Divisor.toQDivisor D₁).QLinearlyEquivalent (Divisor.toQDivisor D₂) := by
  obtain ⟨φ, hφ⟩ := h
  exact ⟨1, one_pos, φ, by rw [← hφ, map_sub, Nat.cast_one, one_smul]⟩

end QLinear

end QDivisor

/-! ### Multiplicity at a point -/

section Multiplicity

/-- The *multiplicity* `mult_x g` of an element `g` of the local ring `𝒪_{X,x}`: the largest
`m ≥ 0` with `g ∈ 𝔪_x^m`. For an effective Cartier divisor `C` with local equation `g` at `x`
this is `mult_x C`; it does not depend on the local equation
(`MMP.Mori.localMultiplicity_mul_of_isUnit`). -/
@[mmp "def_km4a_multiplicity_point"]
def localMultiplicity {x : X} (g : X.presheaf.stalk x) : ℕ∞ :=
  ⨆ (m : ℕ) (_ : g ∈ IsLocalRing.maximalIdeal (X.presheaf.stalk x) ^ m), (m : ℕ∞)

/-- If `g ∈ 𝔪_x^m`, then `m ≤ mult_x g`. -/
theorem le_localMultiplicity {x : X} {g : X.presheaf.stalk x} {m : ℕ}
    (h : g ∈ IsLocalRing.maximalIdeal (X.presheaf.stalk x) ^ m) :
    (m : ℕ∞) ≤ localMultiplicity g :=
  le_iSup₂ (f := fun (m : ℕ) (_ : g ∈ IsLocalRing.maximalIdeal (X.presheaf.stalk x) ^ m) =>
    (m : ℕ∞)) m h

/-- Multiplying `g` by a unit does not change `mult_x g`. -/
theorem localMultiplicity_mul_of_isUnit {x : X} (g : X.presheaf.stalk x)
    {u : X.presheaf.stalk x} (hu : IsUnit u) : localMultiplicity (g * u) = localMultiplicity g := by
  simp only [localMultiplicity, Ideal.mul_unit_mem_iff_mem _ hu]

/-- The *multiplicity* `mult_x P` of a prime divisor `P` at a point `x`: the largest `k ≥ 0` with
`(I_P)_x ⊆ 𝔪_x^k`, where `(I_P)_x ⊆ 𝒪_{X,x}` is the ideal of `P` at `x` and `𝔪_x` the maximal
ideal of `𝒪_{X,x}`. It is `0` if `x ∉ P`
(`MMP.Mori.PrimeDivisor.multiplicityAt_eq_zero_of_notMem`), and it is `mult_x g` for a local
equation `g` of `P` at `x` (`MMP.Mori.PrimeDivisor.multiplicityAt_eq_localMultiplicity`). -/
@[mmp "def_km3a_multiplicity_at_point", mmp "def_km4a_multiplicity_point"]
def PrimeDivisor.multiplicityAt (P : PrimeDivisor X) (x : X) : ℕ∞ :=
  ⨆ (k : ℕ) (_ : P.idealSheaf.stalkIdeal x ≤ IsLocalRing.maximalIdeal (X.presheaf.stalk x) ^ k),
    (k : ℕ∞)

/-- If `g` generates the ideal of `P` at `x`, then `mult_x P = mult_x g`. -/
theorem PrimeDivisor.multiplicityAt_eq_localMultiplicity (P : PrimeDivisor X) {x : X}
    {g : X.presheaf.stalk x} (hg : P.idealSheaf.stalkIdeal x = Ideal.span {g}) :
    P.multiplicityAt x = localMultiplicity g := by
  simp only [multiplicityAt, localMultiplicity, hg, Ideal.span_singleton_le_iff_mem]

/-- A prime divisor has multiplicity `0` at a point outside it. -/
theorem PrimeDivisor.multiplicityAt_eq_zero_of_notMem (P : PrimeDivisor X) {x : X}
    (hx : x ∉ P.support) : P.multiplicityAt x = 0 := by
  rw [multiplicityAt, P.idealSheaf.stalkIdeal_eq_top_of_notMem_support hx]
  refine le_antisymm (iSup₂_le fun k hk => ?_) bot_le
  rcases Nat.eq_zero_or_pos k with rfl | hk0
  · simp
  · exfalso
    have : IsLocalRing.maximalIdeal (X.presheaf.stalk x) ^ k ≤
        IsLocalRing.maximalIdeal (X.presheaf.stalk x) :=
      Ideal.pow_le_self hk0.ne'
    exact (IsLocalRing.maximalIdeal.isMaximal _).ne_top (top_le_iff.mp (hk.trans this))

/-- The *multiplicity* `mult_x D = ∑ dᵢ mult_x Dᵢ` of a divisor `D = ∑ dᵢ Dᵢ` with coefficients
(for instance an effective `ℚ`-divisor) at a point `x`. -/
@[mmp "def_km3a_multiplicity_at_point", mmp "def_km4a_multiplicity_point"]
def DivisorWithCoeffs.multiplicityAt {R : Type v} [AddCommMonoid R] (D : DivisorWithCoeffs R X)
    (x : X) : R :=
  D.sum fun P d => (P.multiplicityAt x).toNat • d

/-- `mult_x (D + D') = mult_x D + mult_x D'`. -/
theorem DivisorWithCoeffs.multiplicityAt_add {R : Type v} [AddCommMonoid R]
    (D D' : DivisorWithCoeffs R X) (x : X) :
    (D + D').multiplicityAt x = D.multiplicityAt x + D'.multiplicityAt x :=
  Finsupp.sum_add_index' (fun _ => smul_zero _) fun _ _ _ => smul_add _ _ _

/-- `mult_x (d P) = d · mult_x P` for a prime divisor `P`. -/
theorem DivisorWithCoeffs.multiplicityAt_single {R : Type v} [AddCommMonoid R]
    (P : PrimeDivisor X) (d : R) (x : X) :
    DivisorWithCoeffs.multiplicityAt (Finsupp.single P d : DivisorWithCoeffs R X) x =
      (P.multiplicityAt x).toNat • d :=
  Finsupp.sum_single_index (smul_zero _)

end Multiplicity

/-! ### Restriction of divisors -/

section Restriction

variable {S : Scheme.{u}}

/-- On a Noetherian scheme `S`, only finitely many prime divisors have their generic point in a
closed subset `T` which contains no generic point of an irreducible component of `S` (no point of
coheight zero): the closure of such a generic point is an irreducible component of `T`. -/
theorem finite_setOf_genericPoint_mem [NoetherianSpace S] {T : Set S} (hT : IsClosed T)
    (h : ∀ s ∈ T, coheight s ≠ 0) : {P : PrimeDivisor S | P.genericPoint ∈ T}.Finite := by
  have hlt : ∀ {a b : S}, a ≤ b → a ≠ b → a < b := fun hab hne ↦
    lt_iff_le_not_ge.mpr ⟨hab, fun h ↦ hne (Specializes.antisymm h hab).eq⟩
  obtain ⟨𝒮, h𝒮fin, h𝒮closed, h𝒮irr, h𝒮cover⟩ :=
    NoetherianSpace.exists_finite_set_isClosed_irreducible hT
  lift 𝒮 to Finset (Set S) using h𝒮fin
  have key : ∀ P : PrimeDivisor S, P.genericPoint ∈ T →
      closure ({P.genericPoint} : Set S) ∈ 𝒮 := by
    intro P hP
    have hzc : coheight P.genericPoint = 1 := P.coheight_genericPoint
    have hcl : closure ({P.genericPoint} : Set S) ⊆ ⋃₀ (𝒮 : Set (Set S)) := by
      rw [← h𝒮cover]
      exact closure_minimal (Set.singleton_subset_iff.mpr hP) hT
    obtain ⟨t, htS, hzt⟩ := isIrreducible_iff_sUnion_isClosed.mp
      isIrreducible_singleton.closure 𝒮 (fun s hs ↦ h𝒮closed s hs) hcl
    set τ := (h𝒮irr t htS).genericPoint
    have hgen : closure ({τ} : Set S) = t :=
      (h𝒮irr t htS).isGenericPoint_genericPoint (h𝒮closed t htS)
    have hτt : τ ∈ t := by rw [← hgen]; exact subset_closure (Set.mem_singleton τ)
    have hτT : τ ∈ T := by
      rw [h𝒮cover]
      exact Set.mem_sUnion_of_mem hτt htS
    have hzmem : P.genericPoint ∈ closure ({τ} : Set S) := by
      rw [hgen]
      exact hzt (subset_closure (Set.mem_singleton _))
    have hzτ : P.genericPoint ≤ τ := specializes_iff_mem_closure.mpr hzmem
    have hz : P.genericPoint = τ := by
      by_contra hne
      have hstep := coheight_add_one_le (hlt hzτ hne)
      rw [hzc] at hstep
      have hτ1 : (1 : ℕ∞) ≤ coheight τ := Order.one_le_iff_ne_zero.mpr (h τ hτT)
      have habs : (2 : ℕ∞) ≤ 1 := by
        refine le_trans ?_ hstep
        rw [show (2 : ℕ∞) = 1 + 1 from rfl]
        gcongr
      exact absurd habs (by decide)
    rw [hz, hgen]
    exact htS
  refine Set.Finite.of_finite_image
    (f := fun P : PrimeDivisor S ↦ closure ({P.genericPoint} : Set S))
    (𝒮.finite_toSet.subset ?_) ?_
  · rintro - ⟨P, hP, rfl⟩
    exact key P hP
  · intro a _ b _ hab
    exact AlgebraicGeometry.PrimeDivisor.genericPoint_injective
      ((show IsGenericPoint a.genericPoint (closure ({b.genericPoint} : Set S)) from hab).eq
        isGenericPoint_closure)

/-- A point of coheight one lying on a prime divisor `E` is the generic point of `E`. -/
theorem PrimeDivisor.eq_genericPoint_of_mem_support (E : PrimeDivisor X) {x : X}
    (hx : x ∈ E.support) (h : coheight x = 1) : x = E.genericPoint := by
  rw [AlgebraicGeometry.PrimeDivisor.support_eq_closure] at hx
  have hle : x ≤ E.genericPoint := specializes_iff_mem_closure.mpr hx
  by_contra hne
  have hlt : x < E.genericPoint :=
    lt_iff_le_not_ge.mpr ⟨hle, fun h' ↦ hne (Specializes.antisymm h' hle).eq⟩
  have hstep := coheight_add_one_le hlt
  rw [h, E.coheight_genericPoint] at hstep
  exact absurd hstep (by decide)

variable (f : S ⟶ X)

/-- The *local intersection length* of a prime divisor `E` of `X` along a prime divisor `P` of
`S`, for a morphism `f : S ⟶ X` (typically the inclusion of a closed subscheme): the length of
the `𝒪_{S,P}`-module `𝒪_{S,P}/I_E 𝒪_{S,P}`, where `I_E 𝒪_{S,P}` is the ideal generated by the
image of the ideal `(I_E)_{f(η_P)}` of `E`. This is the coefficient of `P` in `E|_S`; when `I_E`
is generated by `g` at `f(η_P)` and `𝒪_{S,P}` is a discrete valuation ring, it is the valuation
`v_P(g|_S)`. -/
@[mmp "def_km3a_restriction_to_divisor", mmp "def_km5b_restriction_of_divisor"]
def PrimeDivisor.intersectionLength (E : PrimeDivisor X) (P : PrimeDivisor S) : ℕ :=
  (Module.length (S.presheaf.stalk P.genericPoint)
    (S.presheaf.stalk P.genericPoint ⧸
      (E.idealSheaf.stalkIdeal (f P.genericPoint)).map (f.stalkMap P.genericPoint).hom)).toNat

/-- The local intersection length vanishes along prime divisors of `S` whose generic point does
not map into `E`. -/
theorem PrimeDivisor.intersectionLength_eq_zero_of_notMem (E : PrimeDivisor X)
    {P : PrimeDivisor S} (h : f P.genericPoint ∉ E.support) : E.intersectionLength f P = 0 := by
  rw [intersectionLength, E.idealSheaf.stalkIdeal_eq_top_of_notMem_support h, Ideal.map_top]
  have : Subsingleton (S.presheaf.stalk P.genericPoint ⧸ (⊤ : _root_.Ideal _)) :=
    Ideal.Quotient.subsingleton_iff.mpr rfl
  rw [Module.length_eq_zero]
  rfl

namespace DivisorWithCoeffs

variable {R : Type v} [AddCommMonoid R]

/-- The coefficient `∑ᵢ dᵢ · length(𝒪_{S,P}/I_{Dᵢ}𝒪_{S,P})` of a prime divisor `P` of `S` in the
restriction of `D = ∑ dᵢ Dᵢ` along `f : S ⟶ X`. -/
def restrictCoeff (D : DivisorWithCoeffs R X) (P : PrimeDivisor S) : R :=
  D.sum fun E d => E.intersectionLength f P • d

open Classical in
/-- The *restriction* `D|_S = ∑_P (∑ᵢ dᵢ · length(𝒪_{S,P}/I_{Dᵢ}𝒪_{S,P})) P` of a divisor
`D = ∑ dᵢ Dᵢ` along a morphism `f : S ⟶ X`, typically the inclusion of a closed subscheme
meeting no component of `D` in a component of `S`. The sum is finite under that hypothesis
(`MMP.Mori.DivisorWithCoeffs.finite_support_restrictCoeff`); the restriction is the zero
divisor when it is not. -/
@[mmp "def_km3a_restriction_to_divisor", mmp "def_km5b_restriction_of_divisor"]
def restrict (D : DivisorWithCoeffs R X) : DivisorWithCoeffs R S :=
  if h : (Function.support (restrictCoeff f D)).Finite then Finsupp.ofSupportFinite _ h else 0

/-- When its support is finite, the coefficient of a prime divisor `P` of `S` in `D|_S` is
`∑ᵢ dᵢ · length(𝒪_{S,P}/I_{Dᵢ}𝒪_{S,P})`. -/
theorem coeff_restrict {D : DivisorWithCoeffs R X}
    (h : (Function.support (restrictCoeff f D)).Finite) (P : PrimeDivisor S) :
    (D.restrict f).coeff P = D.sum fun E d => E.intersectionLength f P • d := by
  rw [restrict, dite_eq_left_of_eq_true (eq_true h)]
  rfl

/-- If no generic point of an irreducible component of `S` (no point of coheight zero) maps into
a component of `D`, the restriction of `D` along `f` has finite support. -/
theorem finite_support_restrictCoeff [NoetherianSpace S] (D : DivisorWithCoeffs R X)
    (hD : ∀ E ∈ D.support, ∀ s : S, coheight s = 0 → f s ∉ E.support) :
    (Function.support (restrictCoeff f D)).Finite := by
  refine ((D.support.finite_toSet).biUnion fun E hE => finite_setOf_genericPoint_mem
    (T := f ⁻¹' E.support) (E.idealSheaf.support.isClosed.preimage f.continuous)
    fun s hs h0 => hD E hE s h0 hs).subset ?_
  intro P hP
  obtain ⟨E, hE, hne⟩ := Finset.exists_ne_zero_of_sum_ne_zero hP
  refine Set.mem_iUnion₂.mpr ⟨E, hE, ?_⟩
  by_contra hnot
  apply hne
  change E.intersectionLength f P • D E = 0
  rw [PrimeDivisor.intersectionLength_eq_zero_of_notMem f E hnot, zero_smul]

/-- If `S` has pure codimension one (the generic point of every irreducible component of `S`
maps to a point of coheight one) and no component of `D` is the image of a component of `S`,
then no component of `S` maps into a component of `D`. -/
theorem forall_notMem_support_of_coheight (D : DivisorWithCoeffs R X)
    (hpure : ∀ s : S, coheight s = 0 → coheight (f s) = 1)
    (hD : ∀ E ∈ D.support, ∀ s : S, coheight s = 0 → f s ≠ E.genericPoint) :
    ∀ E ∈ D.support, ∀ s : S, coheight s = 0 → f s ∉ E.support :=
  fun E hE s hs hmem => hD E hE s hs (E.eq_genericPoint_of_mem_support hmem (hpure s hs))

/-- For a morphism `f : S ⟶ X` from a Noetherian scheme of pure codimension one (for instance a
reduced divisor) such that no component of `D` is the image of a component of `S`, the
coefficients of `D|_S` are `∑ᵢ dᵢ · length(𝒪_{S,P}/I_{Dᵢ}𝒪_{S,P})`. -/
theorem coeff_restrict_of_pure [NoetherianSpace S] (D : DivisorWithCoeffs R X)
    (hpure : ∀ s : S, coheight s = 0 → coheight (f s) = 1)
    (hD : ∀ E ∈ D.support, ∀ s : S, coheight s = 0 → f s ≠ E.genericPoint) (P : PrimeDivisor S) :
    (D.restrict f).coeff P = D.sum fun E d => E.intersectionLength f P • d :=
  coeff_restrict f (finite_support_restrictCoeff f D
    (forall_notMem_support_of_coheight f D hpure hD)) P

/-- The *restriction* `B|_F` of a divisor `B = ∑ βᵢ Bᵢ` to a prime divisor `F` of `X`: the
divisor on `F` whose coefficient at a prime divisor `Q` of `F` is
`∑ᵢ βᵢ · length(𝒪_{F,Q}/I_{Bᵢ}𝒪_{F,Q})`. It is well defined when `F` is not a component of `B`
(`MMP.Mori.DivisorWithCoeffs.coeff_restrictPrimeDivisor`). -/
@[mmp "def_km3a_restriction_to_divisor"]
abbrev restrictPrimeDivisor (D : DivisorWithCoeffs R X) (F : PrimeDivisor X) :
    DivisorWithCoeffs R F.idealSheaf.subscheme :=
  D.restrict F.idealSheaf.subschemeι

/-- If `F` is not a component of `D`, no component of `F` maps into a component of `D`. -/
theorem forall_notMem_support_primeDivisor (D : DivisorWithCoeffs R X) (F : PrimeDivisor X)
    (hF : D.coeff F = 0) :
    ∀ E ∈ D.support, ∀ s : F.idealSheaf.subscheme, coheight s = 0 →
      F.idealSheaf.subschemeι s ∉ E.support := by
  intro E hE s hs hmem
  have := F.integral
  have hgen : s = _root_.genericPoint F.idealSheaf.subscheme := by
    have hle : s ≤ _root_.genericPoint F.idealSheaf.subscheme :=
      genericPoint_specializes s
    exact (Specializes.antisymm (coheight_eq_zero.mp hs hle) hle).eq
  have hsF : F.idealSheaf.subschemeι s = F.genericPoint := by
    rw [hgen]
    rfl
  rw [hsF] at hmem
  have hEF := E.eq_genericPoint_of_mem_support hmem F.coheight_genericPoint
  have : F = E := AlgebraicGeometry.PrimeDivisor.genericPoint_injective hEF
  rw [Finsupp.mem_support_iff, ← this] at hE
  exact hE hF

/-- On a Noetherian scheme, the coefficients of the restriction `B|_F` of `B` to a prime divisor
`F` which is not a component of `B` are `∑ᵢ βᵢ · length(𝒪_{F,Q}/I_{Bᵢ}𝒪_{F,Q})`. -/
theorem coeff_restrictPrimeDivisor [NoetherianSpace X] (D : DivisorWithCoeffs R X)
    (F : PrimeDivisor X) (hF : D.coeff F = 0) (Q : PrimeDivisor F.idealSheaf.subscheme) :
    (D.restrictPrimeDivisor F).coeff Q =
      D.sum fun E d => E.intersectionLength F.idealSheaf.subschemeι Q • d :=
  haveI : NoetherianSpace F.idealSheaf.subscheme :=
    F.idealSheaf.subschemeι.isClosedEmbedding.isInducing.noetherianSpace
  coeff_restrict _ (finite_support_restrictCoeff _ D
    (forall_notMem_support_primeDivisor D F hF)) Q

/-- The *local intersection number* `(C · Δ)_x` of a prime divisor `C` (a smooth curve on a
smooth surface) with a divisor `Δ` at a point `x` of `C` (a prime divisor of the curve `C`): the
coefficient of `x` in `Δ|_C`. -/
@[mmp "def_km5b_restriction_of_divisor"]
def localIntersectionNumber (C : PrimeDivisor X) (Δ : DivisorWithCoeffs R X)
    (x : PrimeDivisor C.idealSheaf.subscheme) : R :=
  (Δ.restrictPrimeDivisor C).coeff x

open Classical in
/-- The coefficient `∑_{j : C ⊆ Dⱼ} aⱼ` of a prime divisor `C` of `S` in the restriction by
components of `Δ = ∑ aⱼ Dⱼ` along `f : S ⟶ X`; `C ⊆ Dⱼ` is read as `f(η_C) ∈ Dⱼ`, which is
the same for a closed immersion since `Dⱼ` is closed. -/
def restrictComponentsCoeff (D : DivisorWithCoeffs R X) (C : PrimeDivisor S) : R :=
  D.sum fun E d => if f C.genericPoint ∈ E.support then d else 0

open Classical in
/-- The *restriction* `Δ|_H` of a divisor `Δ = ∑ aⱼ Dⱼ` to a closed subscheme `f : H ⟶ X` of
pure codimension one containing no `Dⱼ`: the divisor on `H` whose coefficient at a prime divisor
`C` of `H` is `∑_{j : C ⊆ Dⱼ} aⱼ`. The sum is finite under that hypothesis
(`MMP.Mori.DivisorWithCoeffs.finite_support_restrictComponentsCoeff`); the restriction is the
zero divisor when it is not. -/
@[mmp "def_km5d_restriction_to_general_member"]
def restrictComponents (D : DivisorWithCoeffs R X) : DivisorWithCoeffs R S :=
  if h : (Function.support (restrictComponentsCoeff f D)).Finite then
    Finsupp.ofSupportFinite _ h
  else 0

open Classical in
/-- When its support is finite, the coefficient of a prime divisor `C` of `S` in `Δ|_S` is
`∑_{j : C ⊆ Dⱼ} aⱼ`. -/
theorem coeff_restrictComponents {D : DivisorWithCoeffs R X}
    (h : (Function.support (restrictComponentsCoeff f D)).Finite) (C : PrimeDivisor S) :
    (D.restrictComponents f).coeff C =
      D.sum fun E d => if f C.genericPoint ∈ E.support then d else 0 := by
  rw [restrictComponents, dite_eq_left_of_eq_true (eq_true h)]
  rfl

/-- If no generic point of an irreducible component of `S` maps into a component of `D`, the
restriction by components of `D` along `f` has finite support. -/
theorem finite_support_restrictComponentsCoeff [NoetherianSpace S] (D : DivisorWithCoeffs R X)
    (hD : ∀ E ∈ D.support, ∀ s : S, coheight s = 0 → f s ∉ E.support) :
    (Function.support (restrictComponentsCoeff f D)).Finite := by
  classical
  refine ((D.support.finite_toSet).biUnion fun E hE => finite_setOf_genericPoint_mem
    (T := f ⁻¹' E.support) (E.idealSheaf.support.isClosed.preimage f.continuous)
    fun s hs h0 => hD E hE s h0 hs).subset ?_
  intro C hC
  obtain ⟨E, hE, hne⟩ := Finset.exists_ne_zero_of_sum_ne_zero hC
  refine Set.mem_iUnion₂.mpr ⟨E, hE, ?_⟩
  by_contra hnot
  exact hne (by simp only [ite_eq_right_iff]; exact fun h => absurd h hnot)

open Classical in
/-- For a closed subscheme `H` of pure codimension one of a Noetherian scheme `X` containing no
component of `Δ`, the coefficients of `Δ|_H` at a prime divisor `C` of `H` are
`∑_{j : C ⊆ Dⱼ} aⱼ`. -/
theorem coeff_restrictComponents_of_pure [NoetherianSpace S] (D : DivisorWithCoeffs R X)
    (hpure : ∀ s : S, coheight s = 0 → coheight (f s) = 1)
    (hD : ∀ E ∈ D.support, E.genericPoint ∉ Set.range f) (C : PrimeDivisor S) :
    (D.restrictComponents f).coeff C =
      D.sum fun E d => if f C.genericPoint ∈ E.support then d else 0 :=
  coeff_restrictComponents f (finite_support_restrictComponentsCoeff f D
    (forall_notMem_support_of_coheight f D hpure fun E hE s _ h => hD E hE ⟨s, h⟩)) C

end DivisorWithCoeffs

end Restriction

/-! ### `K`-Cartier divisors -/

section CartierCombination

/-- The space `Div(X)_K` of *`K`-Cartier divisors* (for `K = ℚ` or `ℝ`) of a locally Noetherian
normal scheme `X`: the free `K`-module on the set of Cartier divisors of `X`, whose elements are
the formal finite `K`-linear combinations `∑ⱼ cⱼ Dⱼ` of Cartier divisors `Dⱼ`. -/
abbrev CartierDivisorWithCoeffs (K : Type v) [Zero K] (X : Scheme.{u}) [IsLocallyNoetherian X]
    [IsNormal X] : Type (max u v) :=
  (Divisor.cartierSubgroup (X := X)) →₀ K

namespace CartierDivisorWithCoeffs

variable {K : Type v} [IsLocallyNoetherian X] [IsNormal X]

/-- A Cartier divisor `D`, regarded as the `K`-Cartier divisor `1 · D`. -/
def ofCartier [Zero K] [One K] (D : Divisor.cartierSubgroup (X := X)) :
    CartierDivisorWithCoeffs K X :=
  Finsupp.single D 1

/-- The *realization* of a `K`-Cartier divisor `∑ⱼ cⱼ Dⱼ` with integral coefficients `cⱼ = nⱼ`:
the Cartier divisor `∑ⱼ nⱼ Dⱼ`, computed in the group of Cartier divisors. -/
def realization [Ring K] (c : CartierDivisorWithCoeffs K X) (h : ∀ D, ∃ n : ℤ, c D = n) :
    Divisor.cartierSubgroup (X := X) :=
  c.sum fun D _ => (h D).choose • D

/-- The *Weil divisor* `∑ⱼ cⱼ Dⱼ` with coefficients in `K` underlying a `K`-Cartier divisor. -/
def toDivisorWithCoeffs [Ring K] : CartierDivisorWithCoeffs K X →+ DivisorWithCoeffs K X :=
  Finsupp.liftAddHom fun D =>
    { toFun := fun r => r • DivisorWithCoeffs.ofDivisor K (D : Divisor X)
      map_zero' := zero_smul _ _
      map_add' := fun _ _ => add_smul _ _ _ }

/-- The `K`-Cartier divisor `r · D` has underlying Weil divisor `r D`. -/
theorem toDivisorWithCoeffs_single [Ring K] (D : Divisor.cartierSubgroup (X := X)) (r : K) :
    toDivisorWithCoeffs (Finsupp.single D r) = r • DivisorWithCoeffs.ofDivisor K (D : Divisor X) :=
  Finsupp.liftAddHom_apply_single _ _ _

/-- A Cartier divisor `1 · D` has underlying Weil divisor `D`. -/
theorem toDivisorWithCoeffs_ofCartier [Ring K] (D : Divisor.cartierSubgroup (X := X)) :
    toDivisorWithCoeffs (ofCartier D : CartierDivisorWithCoeffs K X) =
      DivisorWithCoeffs.ofDivisor K (D : Divisor X) := by
  rw [ofCartier, toDivisorWithCoeffs_single, one_smul]

/-- The realization of an integral `K`-Cartier divisor has the same underlying Weil divisor. -/
theorem ofDivisor_realization [Ring K] (c : CartierDivisorWithCoeffs K X)
    (h : ∀ D, ∃ n : ℤ, c D = n) :
    DivisorWithCoeffs.ofDivisor K ((c.realization h : Divisor.cartierSubgroup (X := X)) :
      Divisor X) = toDivisorWithCoeffs c := by
  change DivisorWithCoeffs.ofDivisor K (Divisor.cartierSubgroup.subtype (c.realization h)) = _
  rw [realization, map_finsuppSum, map_finsuppSum, toDivisorWithCoeffs,
    Finsupp.liftAddHom_apply]
  refine Finsupp.sum_congr fun D _ => ?_
  change DivisorWithCoeffs.ofDivisor K ((h D).choose • (D : Divisor X)) =
    c D • DivisorWithCoeffs.ofDivisor K (D : Divisor X)
  rw [map_zsmul, ← Int.cast_smul_eq_zsmul K]
  exact congrArg (· • _) (h D).choose_spec.symm

end CartierDivisorWithCoeffs

end CartierCombination

namespace QDivisor

variable [IsLocallyNoetherian X] [IsNormal X]

/-- The Cartier divisor `m_D D`, for a `ℚ`-Cartier `ℚ`-divisor `D` with Cartier index `m_D`. -/
def cartierIndexSMul (D : QDivisor X) (h : D.IsQCartier) : Divisor.cartierSubgroup (X := X) :=
  ⟨(isCartierDivisor_cartierIndex_smul h).choose,
    (isCartierDivisor_cartierIndex_smul h).choose_spec.2⟩

/-- The Cartier divisor `m_D D`, regarded as a `ℚ`-divisor, is `m_D · D`. -/
theorem toQDivisor_cartierIndexSMul (D : QDivisor X) (h : D.IsQCartier) :
    Divisor.toQDivisor (D.cartierIndexSMul h : Divisor X) = (D.cartierIndex h : ℤ) • D :=
  (isCartierDivisor_cartierIndex_smul h).choose_spec.1

/-- The *associated `ℚ`-Cartier divisor* `⟨D⟩ = (1/m_D) · (m_D D) ∈ Div(X)_ℚ` of a `ℚ`-Cartier
`ℚ`-divisor `D` with Cartier index `m_D`; Kollár–Mori write `D` for `⟨D⟩`. -/
@[mmp "def_km1b_q_cartier_weil_combination"]
def associatedCartier (D : QDivisor X) (h : D.IsQCartier) : CartierDivisorWithCoeffs ℚ X :=
  (1 / (D.cartierIndex h : ℚ)) • CartierDivisorWithCoeffs.ofCartier (D.cartierIndexSMul h)

/-- The associated `ℚ`-Cartier divisor `⟨D⟩` has underlying `ℚ`-divisor `D`. -/
theorem toDivisorWithCoeffs_associatedCartier (D : QDivisor X) (h : D.IsQCartier) :
    CartierDivisorWithCoeffs.toDivisorWithCoeffs (D.associatedCartier h) = D := by
  rw [associatedCartier, CartierDivisorWithCoeffs.ofCartier, Finsupp.smul_single, smul_eq_mul,
    mul_one, CartierDivisorWithCoeffs.toDivisorWithCoeffs_single]
  change (1 / (D.cartierIndex h : ℚ)) • Divisor.toQDivisor (D.cartierIndexSMul h : Divisor X) = D
  rw [toQDivisor_cartierIndexSMul, ← Int.cast_smul_eq_zsmul ℚ, smul_smul]
  have : (D.cartierIndex h : ℚ) ≠ 0 := Nat.cast_ne_zero.mpr (cartierIndex_pos h).ne'
  push_cast
  rw [one_div_mul_cancel this, one_smul]

end QDivisor

end MMP.Mori
